{"author":{"id":"6d85cf2fcebaeefd8c5c528f2d5f5f98f26ce3275422d0dc5f7c0fd596f9f59f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791595250,"nonce":"hrupgUmbvdXHqn290KRm+AMNa7U=","title":"Inset shadows on a notched box ignore the notch","message":"Inset shadows were built on the padding box's rectangle with no notch, so their ring followed the nominal box, not the notched outline. Reported by the blinc_ts session.\n\n**Change**\nOn a notched node, each inset shadow is drawn on the whole box with the notch, its spread grown by the widest border side, so it starts at the border's inner edge. The border is then drawn again over the shadows, as a node that clips its children already draws its border after them.\n\n**Shader side**\nThe notch's distance function was shallow inside the body: a bulge or peak reached only 8px into it, so an inset ring wider than that showed a seam where they meet. Shaders now let those pieces reach half the body's depth, no wider than at the edge. ashui's Sdf.hx carries that; blinc_ts's sdf.ts and Blinc's notch shader need the same.","files":null}]}